{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"91750cc5-6f7b-4c76-90ea-3ec6d21bf87b","title":"Graphs of y = 2 sin x and y = sin 2x compared"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"91750cc5-6f7b-4c76-90ea-3ec6d21bf87b","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Start with sine as a reference. Its amplitude is one, and one cycle takes two pi along the x-axis.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Compare amplitude and period"},{"op":"axes","id":"axes","region":"right","x":{"min":0,"max":6.283185307179586,"label":"x (radians)"},"y":{"min":-2.5,"max":2.5,"label":"y"}},{"op":"curve","id":"reference","axes_id":"axes","expr":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.283185307179586]},{"op":"equation","id":"base","region":"A2","latex":"y=\\sin x:\\quad A=1,\\quad T=2\\pi"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"91750cc5-6f7b-4c76-90ea-3ec6d21bf87b","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Multiplying sine by two doubles every height. The peaks reach two, but their horizontal positions and the period stay unchanged.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"doubleheight","axes_id":"axes","expr":"2*sin(x)","domain":[0,6.283185307179586]},{"op":"equation","id":"heightformula","region":"B1","latex":"y=2\\sin x"},{"op":"equation","id":"heightfacts","anchor":{"el":"heightformula","side":"below","gap":0.06},"latex":"A=2,\\quad T=2\\pi"},{"op":"point","id":"highpeak","construct":{"kind":"along","element_id":"reference","t":0.25},"label":"reference peak"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"91750cc5-6f7b-4c76-90ea-3ec6d21bf87b","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Putting two inside sine compresses the graph horizontally. Two complete cycles now fit into two pi, while the amplitude remains one.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"doublefreq","axes_id":"axes","expr":"sin(2*x)","domain":[0,6.283185307179586]},{"op":"equation","id":"freqformula","region":"B2","latex":"y=\\sin(2x)"},{"op":"equation","id":"freqfacts","anchor":{"el":"freqformula","side":"below","gap":0.06},"latex":"A=1,\\quad T=\\pi"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which graph has taller peaks, and which completes more cycles from zero to two pi?","expected_gist":"2 sin x has taller peaks; sin 2x completes more cycles."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"91750cc5-6f7b-4c76-90ea-3ec6d21bf87b","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Compare their first peaks: two outside changes height; two inside changes horizontal spacing. In general, amplitude is absolute a and period is two pi over absolute b.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"tallpeak","construct":{"kind":"along","element_id":"doubleheight","t":0.25},"label":"(π/2, 2)"},{"op":"point","id":"earlypeak","construct":{"kind":"along","element_id":"doublefreq","t":0.125},"label":"(π/4, 1)"},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","region":"A3","latex":"y=a\\sin(bx):\\quad A=|a|,\\quad T=\\frac{2\\pi}{|b|}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
